# @HDF5_PACKAGE_NAME@ @HDF5_PACKAGE_VERSION_STRING@

This directory contains a binary distribution built on `@BINARY_PLATFORM@`.
The exact enabled libraries, language wrappers, filters, tools, and other
features are recorded in `libhdf5.settings` in the installed library
directory. That generated file is authoritative; optional products are not
assumed to be present.

The distribution contains either an installer or a compressed package named
for version `@HDF5_PACKAGE_VERSION@` and system `@BINARY_SYSTEM_NAME@`, plus
this README and the project license.

## Installation

Run the platform installer when one is supplied, or extract the compressed
package to the desired prefix. When shared libraries are used, make the
installed runtime directory visible to the operating-system loader.

## Verifying the Installation

The `HDF5Examples` directory is a standalone CMake project that can locate the
installed CMake package and exercise the components that were built. Its
presets and manual workflow are documented in `USING_CMake_Examples.md` in the
documentation directory. No fixed test count is expected because it varies
with the installed feature set.

Current upstream API documentation is available at
https://support.hdfgroup.org/documentation/hdf5/latest/. Upstream release
artifacts and versioned documentation are published at
https://github.com/HDFGroup/hdf5/releases.

Report upstream HDF5 problems through https://help.hdfgroup.org/.
